It is lunchtime now.
I walk outside from the office.
I want an Indian SIM card.
I go to a nearby mobile shop.
There is no big crowd in the shop.
I speak to the shopkeeper.
"Hello, I want a new SIM card," I say.
The shopkeeper gives me a form.
I write my name on the form.
"Does Madam have an ID card?" the shopkeeper asks.
"Yes, I have a passport," I reply.
"How old is Madam?" he asks.
"I am thirty-one years old," I say.
I write it on the form.
He looks at my passport.
The new SIM card is three hundred rupees.
I give the money.
